§ `General conditions`
-- src:60 | ĐIỀU KIỆN CHUNG

§§ `General Condition 1 — conditions precedent`

-- "The Insured's due observance and fulfilment of the terms of this Policy as to what the
-- Insured is obliged to do or perform, and the declarations answering the questions in the
-- questionnaire and the proposal form, shall be conditions precedent to binding Bao Minh's
-- liability to indemnify."
--
-- Two things follow, both on the words and both harsh:
-- * EVERY duty is a condition precedent. Nothing asks whether the breach mattered or caused
--   the loss (Finding 3), and Article 1's undertaking to adjust the sum insured is one of
--   them, which makes the average condition redundant (Finding 4).
-- * The questionnaire limb. Reading (i): the condition is that the questions were ANSWERED.
--   Reading (ii): "chấp hành đúng" (observe correctly) carries over, and the condition is
--   that the answers were TRUE AND COMPLETE. The rules take (ii), which the grammar allows
--   and the purpose of the clause needs; (i) is kept as a named reading (fork F04). Under
--   (ii) there is no test of materiality, intent or connection with the loss (Finding 2).
-- src:62 | 1. Việc Người được bảo hiểm tuân thủ và chấp hành đúng các Điều khoản của Đơn bảo hiểm này
