-- "In any case, Bao Minh will not be liable for loss or liability if, within 14 days from
-- the day of the occurrence, Bao Minh has not RECEIVED notice of the loss."
--
-- Days are calendar days (the document does not say; fork F13). The day of the occurrence
-- is not counted, so notice received on the 14th day after it is in time and on the 15th
-- is not. The period runs from the occurrence, not from when the Insured learned of it
-- (Finding 1).
-- src:109 | Trong mọi trường hợp, Bảo Minh sẽ không chịu trách nhiệm đối với tổn thất hay trách nhiệm,
-- src:110 | nếu trong vòng 14 ngày kể từ ngày xảy ra sự cố Bảo Minh không nhận được thông báo tổn
-- src:111 | thất.
@ref Bao Minh EAR rules, General Condition 5, 14-day bar (src:109-111)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days General Condition 5 allows for Bao Minh to receive notice` MEANS 14

@ref Bao Minh EAR rules, General Condition 5, 14-day bar (src:109-111)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`fourteen days have not yet passed since the occurrence, and no notice has been received` MEANS
    REFUSE "fourteen days have not yet passed since the occurrence, and no notice has been received"

@ref Bao Minh EAR rules, General Condition 5, 14-day bar (src:109-111)
GIVEN `the claim` IS A `A claim`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`General Condition 5: Bao Minh received notice in time of` `the claim` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the claim`'s `the date Bao Minh received notice`
    WHEN JUST r  THEN Day r MINUS Day `the day of the occurrence` AT MOST `the days General Condition 5 allows for Bao Minh to receive notice`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        IF   Day (`the claim`'s `the date of assessment`) MINUS Day `the day of the occurrence` GREATER THAN `the days General Condition 5 allows for Bao Minh to receive notice`
        THEN FALSE
        ELSE `fourteen days have not yet passed since the occurrence, and no notice has been received`
    WHERE `the day of the occurrence` MEANS `the claim`'s `the occurrence`'s `date`

-- "After notifying Bao Minh under this condition, the Insured may repair or replace minor
-- damage. In every other case Bao Minh's representative will be present to inspect the
-- loss before repair or replacement. If Bao Minh's representative does not inspect within
-- a time considered reasonable in the circumstances, the Insured may proceed with the
-- repair or replacement." The sequence is a regulative rule in bm-ear-duties.l4. As a duty
-- (not to repair first) it is implied, not stated (fork F11). "Minor" and "a reasonable
-- time" are not defined (Finding 12).
