GIVEN `the dispute` IS A `The dispute about the claim`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`General Condition 7 does not bar an action against Bao Minh on` `the dispute` MEANS
    IF   `the dispute`'s `liability admitted and the amount disputed`
    THEN isJust (`the dispute`'s `date of the arbitral award`)
    ELSE TRUE

§§ `General Condition 8 — fraud, and the three-month bar`

-- "If any claim is fraudulent or any false declaration is made or used in support of it,
-- or if the Insured or anyone on its behalf uses fraudulent means or devices to gain any
-- benefit under this Policy, ... all benefits under this Policy are of no value."
-- Forfeiture reaches every benefit, not only the fraudulent claim (Finding 16).
-- src:141 | 8. Nếu có sự khiếu nại gian lận hay khai báo sai (được đưa ra hay hỗ trợ cho khiếu nại đó) hay
-- src:142 | nếu Người được bảo hiểm hoặc Người thay mặt họ sử dụng những phương tiện hay thủ đoạn
-- src:143 | gian lận nhằm kiếm lời qua Đơn bảo hiểm này hoặc nếu khiếu nại đòi bồi thường bị khước từ
@ref Bao Minh EAR rules, General Condition 8, first limbs (src:141-143, 146)
GIVEN `the conduct` IS A `The conduct of the Insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`General Condition 8: all benefit is forfeited for` `the conduct` MEANS
       `the conduct`'s `a claim under the policy was fraudulent`
    OR `the conduct`'s `a false declaration was made or used in support of a claim`
    OR `the conduct`'s `fraudulent means or devices were used to obtain a benefit under the policy`

-- "... or if a claim is rejected and no proceedings are commenced within three months from
-- when the two arbitrators or the single arbitrator made their award, in the case of
-- arbitration as provided above, ..."
--
-- As translated the clause has ONE starting point, the award. It does not say "three
-- months after the rejection", so a rejected claim that never went to arbitration is not
-- barred by it (fork F19; Finding 6). Three months are calendar months, as in GC7.
